x}(yx^{2}) = x^{2} \\cdot 2xe^{-x^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186087272} {:answer/id #uuid "6e285ba0-0b5f-5e5a-a7bd-e5b3de551a8e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}(ye^{x^{2}}) = e^{x^{2}} \\cdot 2xe^{-x^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186087273} {:answer/id #uuid "76e91a95-c637-5848-86e4-e944f3eee17e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}(yx) = x \\cdot 2xe^{-x^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186087274}] :answer-field/id #uuid "9f8fe340-5770-5791-befc-e802db4415ea" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186087269}] :question/id #uuid "8973fb88-5098-5e4b-a0b0-25638565dd93" :question/math-academy-id "q-8546" :question/problem "Consider the following first-order linear ODE for the function $y = y(x)$:\n$\\frac{dy}{dx} + 2xy = 2xe^{-x^{2}}$\nWrite the equation in the form $\\frac{d}{dx}(yI(x)) = I(x)Q(x)$, where $I(x)$ is an integrating factor."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284734 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "06e163d8-4a78-504d-8269-402a0415e08e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}(y\\cdot 2x)=2x\\cdot x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281750} {:answer/id #uuid "4382d319-73fb-5cb1-9dfc-25d3c057b161" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}(y{e}^{x})={e}^{x}\\cdot x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282265} {:answer/id #uuid "6ff9a224-fab5-5e91-b0ff-979e6a4e2c7d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}(y\\cdot 2)=2x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282648} {:answer/id #uuid "bae778d3-7532-5194-9c25-d299082a3153" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}(y{e}^{2x})={e}^{2x}\\cdot x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283301} {:answer/id #uuid "c179d6ec-3d07-5033-ad1d-7ca1e0d4284e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}(yx)=x\\cdot x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283370}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4382d319-73fb-5cb1-9dfc-25d3c057b161" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}(y{e}^{x})={e}^{x}\\cdot x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282265} :answer-field/id #uuid "4288ef37-6c06-5c5f-a10c-1e0e96591b46" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284042}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "65a9092a-d6a6-5192-82ca-c04151a6438f" :question/math-academy-id "q-17533" :question/problem "Consider the following first-order linear ODE for the function $y=y(x):$\n\n$$\nx\\frac{dy}{dx}+xy={x}^{2}\n$$\n\nWrite the equation in the form $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(yI(x))=I(x)Q(x),$ where $I(x)$ is an integrating factor." :question/worked-solution "First, we write the equation in standard form. This gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}+y=x.\n$$\n\nThis equation is in the standard form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)y=Q(x)\n$$\n\nwith $P(x)=1$ and $Q(x)=x.$ We proceed to find an integrating factor $I(x)$ using the definition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x) & ={e}^{\\int P(x)\\,dx} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\int 1\\,dx} \\\\  & ={e}^{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply our differential equation through by $I(x)={e}^{x}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{x}\\cdot (\\frac{dy}{dx}+y) & ={e}^{x}\\cdot x \\\\ {e}^{x}\\frac{dy}{dx}+{e}^{x}y & ={e}^{x}\\cdot x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we rewrite the left hand side as $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y\\cdot I(x)):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{d}{dx}(y{e}^{x}) & ={e}^{x}\\cdot x\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284738 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "217ccf45-8734-56ec-b06d-0fa3666f9d6e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}(y{e}^{x})={e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281985} {:answer/id #uuid "610a3a60-2d25-5e70-9070-a40fd0b17bcf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}(y{x}^{2})={x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282515} {:answer/id #uuid "692ebc86-2eeb-51e8-909d-911b7bbb78b9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}(yx)=x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282591} {:answer/id #uuid "887e5de7-cd20-589e-9062-1ed36efe796c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}(y{e}^{-x})={e}^{-x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282865} {:answer/id #uuid "99833182-f1d2-5cc1-b043-ddfe57635bc3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}(y\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283025}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "692ebc86-2eeb-51e8-909d-911b7bbb78b9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}(yx)=x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282591} :answer-field/id #uuid "dd94faa5-6de0-52b0-a454-db6562b0e660" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284320}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0dcacbda-1dc5-5146-b0bc-75c7bab3748d" :question/math-academy-id "q-17539" :question/problem "Consider the following first-order linear ODE for the function $y=y(x):$\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}\\frac{dy}{dx}+xy={x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x,\\,x>0\n$$\n\nWrite the equation in the form $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(yI(x))=I(x)Q(x),$ where $I(x)$ is an integrating factor." :question/worked-solution "First, we write the equation in standard form. This gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}+\\frac{1}{x}\\cdot y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\n$$\n\nThis equation is in the standard form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)y=Q(x)\n$$\n\nwith $P(x)=\\frac{1}{x}$ and $Q(x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.$ We proceed to find an integrating factor $I(x)$ using the definition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x) & ={e}^{\\int P(x)dx} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\int (1/x)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x} \\\\  & =x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply our differential equation through by $I(x)=x$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x\\cdot (\\frac{dy}{dx}+\\frac{1}{x}\\cdot y) & =x\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡x \\\\ x\\cdot \\frac{dy}{dx}+y & =x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we rewrite the left hand side as $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y\\cdot I(x)):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{d}{dx}(yx) & =x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186311565 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "63e2b089-092a-5eca-9f7e-bf626ffedb03" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}(y{e}^{-x/2})={e}^{-x/2}\\cdot {x}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309516} {:answer/id #uuid "71425229-5e0c-56e4-a3c5-6da6bfb56a55" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}(y{e}^{x/2})={e}^{x/2}\\cdot {x}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309627} {:answer/id #uuid "cd378351-ace0-5392-8e0c-b064ad6a0d66" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}(y\\cdot (-\\frac{x}{2}))=-\\frac{x}{2}\\cdot {x}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310393} {:answer/id #uuid "e71cd363-dab5-57e2-b1a7-f9cdab639247" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}(y\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{2}))=-\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot {x}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310584} {:answer/id #uuid "f08a16be-ff29-5897-9836-28db90a5052f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}(y\\cdot 2)=2{x}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310665}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "63e2b089-092a-5eca-9f7e-bf626ffedb03" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}(y{e}^{-x/2})={e}^{-x/2}\\cdot {x}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309516} :answer-field/id #uuid "b03a098b-971d-55f6-a30b-4a30fe70ddf7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311307}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "dba525fe-7e4d-5319-88bd-1b806feb0904" :question/math-academy-id "q-335278" :question/problem "Consider the following first-order linear ODE for the function $y=y(x):$\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}-\\frac{1}{2}y={x}^{3}\n$$\n\nWrite the equation in the form $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(yI(x))=I(x)Q(x),$ where $I(x)$ is an integrating factor." :question/worked-solution "This equation is in the standard form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)y=Q(x)\n$$\n\nwith $P(x)=-\\frac{1}{2}$ and $Q(x)={x}^{3}.$ We proceed to find an integrating factor $I(x)$ using the definition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x) & ={e}^{\\int P(x)\\,dx} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\int (-1/2)\\,dx} \\\\  & ={e}^{-x/2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply our differential equation through by $I(x)={e}^{-x/2}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-x/2}\\cdot (\\frac{dy}{dx}-\\frac{1}{2}y) & ={e}^{-x/2}\\cdot {x}^{3} \\\\ {e}^{-x/2}\\cdot \\frac{dy}{dx}+\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{-x/2}\\cdot y & ={e}^{-x/2}\\cdot {x}^{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we rewrite the left hand side as $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y\\cdot I(x)):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{d}{dx}(y{e}^{-x/2}) & ={e}^{-x/2}\\cdot {x}^{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186348294 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "205e27b5-4aef-53eb-8cf0-e7365d5f4c57" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y{x}^{2})={x}^{2}{e}^{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186345637} {:answer/id #uuid "7510063a-6cf7-5663-bf6a-5afc7e2ed0eb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y{e}^{x})={e}^{x}{e}^{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346382} {:answer/id #uuid "8483449c-5ecd-5c41-92e1-0ded8b81ec2c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y{e}^{-x})={e}^{-x}{e}^{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346505} {:answer/id #uuid "b9c267a8-32e4-55c8-8af3-388216c0c46a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(yx)=x{e}^{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346964} {:answer/id #uuid "cf856d8b-bb28-5fc8-bf77-c77ea36fa1c6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\cdot {e}^{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347167}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b9c267a8-32e4-55c8-8af3-388216c0c46a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(yx)=x{e}^{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346964} :answer-field/id #uuid "6b3a3107-9d3a-5db2-9a74-94dd3b070895" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347795}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7613e649-714b-58e4-9ccc-7a0b944dc47c" :question/math-academy-id "q-79818" :question/problem "Consider the following first-order linear ODE for the function $y=y(x):$\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{1}{x}\\cdot y={e}^{x},\\,x>0\n$$\n\nWrite the equation in the form $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(yI(x))=I(x)Q(x),$ where $I(x)$ is an integrating factor." :question/worked-solution "This equation is in the standard form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)y=Q(x)\n$$\n\nwith $P(x)=\\frac{1}{x}$ and $Q(x)={e}^{x}.$ We proceed to find an integrating factor $I(x)$ using the definition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x) & ={e}^{\\int P(x)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\int (1/x)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x} \\\\  & =x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply our differential equation through by $I(x)=x$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x\\cdot (\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{1}{x}\\cdot y) & =x\\cdot {e}^{x} \\\\ x\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+y & =x{e}^{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we rewrite the left hand side as $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y\\cdot I(x)):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(yx) & =x{e}^{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186348295 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "89cf29a8-7002-55ea-90d8-6e36bd328018" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\cdot \\frac{1}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346547} {:answer/id #uuid "bbbc1949-1dc3-5132-b9a6-2f5a02db8b43" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y{x}^{2})={x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346980} {:answer/id #uuid "c06aae51-d699-5f08-973e-040bd676bd09" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y{e}^{x})={e}^{x}\\cdot \\frac{1}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347016} {:answer/id #uuid "d0fb694c-f9b1-5dce-86ee-87c1b3194d74" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(yx)=x\\cdot \\frac{1}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347181} {:answer/id #uuid "f0d204d7-b947-5d35-bd31-8a40d4cc447b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y\\cdot 2)=2\\cdot \\frac{1}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347475}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bbbc1949-1dc3-5132-b9a6-2f5a02db8b43" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y{x}^{2})={x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346980} :answer-field/id #uuid "b92de6c6-2fc5-5d10-b5ab-f609af76b489" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347930}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2870a84c-606f-5fc5-a1ed-a94d670c16ed" :question/math-academy-id "q-79819" :question/problem "Consider the following first-order linear ODE for the function $y=y(x):$\n\n$$\nx\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+2y=1\n$$\n\nWrite the equation in the form $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(yI(x))=I(x)Q(x),$ where $I(x)$ is an integrating factor." :question/worked-solution "First, we write the equation in standard form. This gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{2}{x}\\cdot y=\\frac{1}{x}.\n$$\n\nThis equation is in the standard form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)y=Q(x)\n$$\n\nwith $P(x)=\\frac{2}{x}$ and $Q(x)=\\frac{1}{x}.$ We proceed to find an integrating factor $I(x)$ using the definition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x) & ={e}^{\\int P(x)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\int (2/x)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2})} \\\\  & ={x}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply our differential equation through by $I(x)={x}^{2}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}\\cdot (\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{2}{x}\\cdot y) & ={x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{x} \\\\ {x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+2xy & ={x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we rewrite the left hand side as $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y\\cdot I(x)):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y{x}^{2}) & ={x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186435867 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0b978ec0-c1dc-593e-85ec-c512eb8b8bba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}(y\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2x|)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2x|\\operatorname{sin}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435832} {:answer/id #uuid "1da376ec-fadc-58b2-9050-98c3a0e3289d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}(y{x}^{2})={x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435835} {:answer/id #uuid "39544074-ae02-530d-9e3a-2a0b0340a99a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}(y{e}^{2x})={e}^{2x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435838} {:answer/id #uuid "97ed5649-7d28-5597-8785-b502fbbd5161" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}(y\\cdot 2x)=2x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435845} {:answer/id #uuid "a6707d7d-a941-50a8-9de7-4cedeafd40fc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}(y{e}^{{x}^{2}})={e}^{{x}^{2}}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435847}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a6707d7d-a941-50a8-9de7-4cedeafd40fc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}(y{e}^{{x}^{2}})={e}^{{x}^{2}}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435847} :answer-field/id #uuid "7bf5e5ce-2a24-563a-8eed-d37940cab8bf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435863}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "73fd6309-052f-5dd1-8e4c-82525a25d454" :question/math-academy-id "q-335274" :question/problem "Consider the following first-order linear ODE for the function $y=y(x):$\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}+2xy=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\n$$\n\nWrite the equation in the form $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(yI(x))=I(x)Q(x),$ where $I(x)$ is an integrating factor." :question/worked-solution "This equation is in the standard form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)y=Q(x)\n$$\n\nwith $P(x)=2x$ and $Q(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.$ We proceed to find an integrating factor $I(x)$ using the definition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x) & ={e}^{\\int P(x)\\,dx} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\int 2x\\,dx} \\\\  & ={e}^{{x}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply our differential equation through by $I(x)={e}^{{x}^{2}}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{{x}^{2}}\\cdot (\\frac{dy}{dx}+2xy) & ={e}^{{x}^{2}}\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡x \\\\ {e}^{{x}^{2}}\\cdot \\frac{dy}{dx}+2x{e}^{{x}^{2}}\\cdot y & ={e}^{{x}^{2}}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we rewrite the left hand side as $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y\\cdot I(x)):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{d}{dx}(y{e}^{{x}^{2}}) & ={e}^{{x}^{2}}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186495312 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9883db31-c965-5a25-a3db-2fe7202d1718" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(y\\cdot \\left(x^{2}\\right)\\right)=\\left(x^{2}\\right)\\cdot \\left(x^{3}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495347} {:answer/id #uuid "acd0d970-3e90-555a-961f-735eefa2db11" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(y\\cdot \\left(e^{- 3 x}\\right)\\right)=\\left(e^{- 3 x}\\right)\\cdot \\left(x^{3}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495353} {:answer/id #uuid "cdff44bf-d414-52e1-adf1-e4edbb9765ae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(y\\cdot \\left(e^{3 x}\\right)\\right)=\\left(e^{3 x}\\right)\\cdot \\left(x^{3}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495361} {:answer/id #uuid "f28fc0f9-3e8d-5e9f-b499-4bccbcb13076" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(y\\cdot \\left(e^{6 x}\\right)\\right)=\\left(e^{6 x}\\right)\\cdot \\left(x^{3}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495369} {:answer/id #uuid "fee4d65e-8697-59f0-8f1d-ea6283a9d22c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(y\\cdot \\left(x\\right)\\right)=\\left(x\\right)\\cdot \\left(x^{3}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495374}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cdff44bf-d414-52e1-adf1-e4edbb9765ae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(y\\cdot \\left(e^{3 x}\\right)\\right)=\\left(e^{3 x}\\right)\\cdot \\left(x^{3}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495361} :answer-field/id #uuid "b9b5c6eb-3118-5eb5-9108-444148635772" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495357}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "03f01512-4546-59df-8e70-3aa004e3020a" :question/problem "Consider the following first-order linear ODE for the function $y=y(x):$\n\n$$\n\\left(x\\right)\\cdot \\frac{dy}{dx}+\\left(3 x\\right)\\cdot y=x^{4}\n$$\n\nWrite the equation in the form $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(yI(x))=I(x)Q(x),$ where $I(x)$ is an integrating factor.\n\nAssume $x>0$." :question/worked-solution "First, we write the equation in standard form. This gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}+\\left(3\\right)\\cdot y=x^{3}.\n$$\n\nThis equation is in the standard form\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}+P(x)y=Q(x)\n$$\n\nwith $P(x)=3$ and $Q(x)=x^{3}.$ We proceed to find an integrating factor $I(x)$ using the definition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x) & =e^{\\int P(x)\\,dx} \\\\  & =e^{\\int \\left(3\\right)\\,dx} \\\\  & =e^{3 x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply our differential equation through by $I(x)=e^{3 x}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\left(e^{3 x}\\right)\\cdot \\left(\\frac{dy}{dx}+\\left(3\\right)\\cdot y\\right) & =\\left(e^{3 x}\\right)\\cdot \\left(x^{3}\\right) \\\\ \\left(e^{3 x}\\right)\\cdot \\frac{dy}{dx}+\\left(3\\right)\\cdot \\left(e^{3 x}\\right)\\cdot y & =\\left(e^{3 x}\\right)\\cdot \\left(x^{3}\\right)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we rewrite the left hand side as $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y\\cdot I(x)):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(y\\cdot \\left(e^{3 x}\\right)\\right) & =\\left(e^{3 x}\\right)\\cdot \\left(x^{3}\\right)\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186495315 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "223242e6-657c-5bec-8429-628abde472df" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(y\\cdot \\left(x\\right)\\right)=\\left(x\\right)\\cdot \\left(\\cos{\\left(3 x \\right)}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495317} {:answer/id #uuid "2616a25d-dc53-5253-a481-88bfdb77dd30" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(y\\cdot \\left(e^{- 2 x}\\right)\\right)=\\left(e^{- 2 x}\\right)\\cdot \\left(\\cos{\\left(3 x \\right)}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495319} {:answer/id #uuid "2824925e-5b26-5a3d-ac14-d9fecafbcf4a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(y\\cdot \\left(e^{- x}\\right)\\right)=\\left(e^{- x}\\right)\\cdot \\left(\\cos{\\left(3 x \\right)}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495320} {:answer/id #uuid "91e8878f-4919-5880-ad79-fe8271c9a55c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(y\\cdot \\left(e^{x}\\right)\\right)=\\left(e^{x}\\right)\\cdot \\left(\\cos{\\left(3 x \\right)}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495345} {:answer/id #uuid "b97d76c6-b915-54b0-bcf7-c2824c4dd262" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(y\\cdot \\left(x^{2}\\right)\\right)=\\left(x^{2}\\right)\\cdot \\left(\\cos{\\left(3 x \\right)}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495356}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2824925e-5b26-5a3d-ac14-d9fecafbcf4a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(y\\cdot \\left(e^{- x}\\right)\\right)=\\left(e^{- x}\\right)\\cdot \\left(\\cos{\\left(3 x \\right)}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495320} :answer-field/id #uuid "4d3a783d-5c90-57dd-b22c-25811200de97" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495325}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1fa0b599-1031-5002-a477-8a20611908f9" :question/problem "Consider the following first-order linear ODE for the function $y = y(x)$:\n$\\frac{dy}{dx}-y=\\cos{\\left(3 x \\right)}$\nWrite the equation in the form $\\frac{d}{dx}(yI(x)) = I(x)Q(x)$, where $I(x)$ is an integrating factor." :question/worked-solution "This equation is in the standard form\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}+P(x)y=Q(x)\n$$\n\nwith $P(x)=-1$ and $Q(x)=\\cos{\\left(3 x \\right)}.$ We proceed to find an integrating factor $I(x)$ using the definition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x) & =e^{\\int P(x)\\,dx} \\\\  & =e^{\\int \\left(-1\\right)\\,dx} \\\\  & =e^{- x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply our differential equation through by $I(x)=e^{- x}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\left(e^{- x}\\right)\\cdot \\left(\\frac{dy}{dx}-y\\right) & =\\left(e^{- x}\\right)\\cdot \\left(\\cos{\\left(3 x \\right)}\\right) \\\\ \\left(e^{- x}\\right)\\cdot \\frac{dy}{dx}-\\left(1\\right)\\cdot \\left(e^{- x}\\right)\\cdot y & =\\left(e^{- x}\\right)\\cdot \\left(\\cos{\\left(3 x \\right)}\\right)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we rewrite the left hand side as $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y\\cdot I(x)):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(y\\cdot \\left(e^{- x}\\right)\\right) & =\\left(e^{- x}\\right)\\cdot \\left(\\cos{\\left(3 x \\right)}\\right)\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186495321 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "52024f4a-ebc0-5103-a1e8-78758bc1c99d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(y\\cdot \\left(e^{4 x}\\right)\\right)=\\left(e^{4 x}\\right)\\cdot \\left(2 x e^{- 2 x^{2}}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495327} {:answer/id #uuid "74506bb6-4469-5ca5-9318-2f49b6ac1c05" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(y\\cdot \\left(e^{2 x}\\right)\\right)=\\left(e^{2 x}\\right)\\cdot \\left(2 x e^{- 2 x^{2}}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495336} {:answer/id #uuid "7d011e5a-cc83-508a-8044-57460dbf6338" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(y\\cdot \\left(x^{2}\\right)\\right)=\\left(x^{2}\\right)\\cdot \\left(2 x e^{- 2 x^{2}}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495339} {:answer/id #uuid "7e771ef1-20d6-5648-a90c-5a9d67f6ba18" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(y\\cdot \\left(e^{- 2 x^{2}}\\right)\\right)=\\left(e^{- 2 x^{2}}\\right)\\cdot \\left(2 x e^{- 2 x^{2}}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495341} {:answer/id #uuid "fd771fd1-9b4f-586e-8ed4-087edb576c3e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(y\\cdot \\left(e^{2 x^{2}}\\right)\\right)=\\left(e^{2 x^{2}}\\right)\\cdot \\left(2 x e^{- 2 x^{2}}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495371}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fd771fd1-9b4f-586e-8ed4-087edb576c3e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(y\\cdot \\left(e^{2 x^{2}}\\right)\\right)=\\left(e^{2 x^{2}}\\right)\\cdot \\left(2 x e^{- 2 x^{2}}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495371} :answer-field/id #uuid "2964e3c2-a14e-55dd-ac21-39c9a0f77011" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495322}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "2828617e-8430-5e95-bfed-6d4734e5a2e6" :question/problem "Consider the following first-order linear ODE for the function $y=y(x):$\n\n$$\n\\left(3\\right)\\cdot \\frac{dy}{dx}+\\left(12 x\\right)\\cdot y=6 x e^{- 2 x^{2}}\n$$\n\nWrite the equation in the form $\\frac{d}{dx}(yI(x))=I(x)Q(x),$ where $I(x)$ is an integrating factor." :question/worked-solution "First, we write the equation in standard form. This gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}+\\left(4 x\\right)\\cdot y=2 x e^{- 2 x^{2}}.\n$$\n\nThis equation is in the standard form\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}+P(x)y=Q(x)\n$$\n\nwith $P(x)=4 x$ and $Q(x)=2 x e^{- 2 x^{2}}.$ We proceed to find an integrating factor $I(x)$ using the definition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x) & =e^{\\int P(x)\\,dx} \\\\  & =e^{\\int \\left(4 x\\right)\\,dx} \\\\  & =e^{2 x^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply our differential equation through by $I(x)=e^{2 x^{2}}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\left(e^{2 x^{2}}\\right)\\cdot \\left(\\frac{dy}{dx}+\\left(4 x\\right)\\cdot y\\right) & =\\left(e^{2 x^{2}}\\right)\\cdot \\left(2 x e^{- 2 x^{2}}\\right) \\\\ \\left(e^{2 x^{2}}\\right)\\cdot \\frac{dy}{dx}+\\left(4 x\\right)\\cdot \\left(e^{2 x^{2}}\\right)\\cdot y & =\\left(e^{2 x^{2}}\\right)\\cdot \\left(2 x e^{- 2 x^{2}}\\right)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we rewrite the left hand side as $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y\\cdot I(x)):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(y\\cdot \\left(e^{2 x^{2}}\\right)\\right) & =\\left(e^{2 x^{2}}\\right)\\cdot \\left(2 x e^{- 2 x^{2}}\\right)\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186495328 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "59eeb590-79fd-58f7-ad78-207852a155dc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(y\\cdot \\left(e^{3 x^{2}}\\right)\\right)=\\left(e^{3 x^{2}}\\right)\\cdot \\left(2 x e^{3 x^{2}}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495330} {:answer/id #uuid "68f5ac64-b832-5951-bffe-8ffd8ba5cf8c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(y\\cdot \\left(e^{- 3 x^{2}}\\right)\\right)=\\left(e^{- 3 x^{2}}\\right)\\cdot \\left(2 x e^{3 x^{2}}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495332} {:answer/id #uuid "7de2f377-86ef-5ea6-a299-49f2f2a98bf4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(y\\cdot \\left(x^{2}\\right)\\right)=\\left(x^{2}\\right)\\cdot \\left(2 x e^{3 x^{2}}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495340} {:answer/id #uuid "84fe84eb-4e89-56b7-9e40-585553aea026" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(y\\cdot \\left(e^{6 x}\\right)\\right)=\\left(e^{6 x}\\right)\\cdot \\left(2 x e^{3 x^{2}}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495342} {:answer/id #uuid "e2217242-e42e-5522-8af0-a8daa9849881" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(y\\cdot \\left(e^{3 x}\\right)\\right)=\\left(e^{3 x}\\right)