ft(2 x e^{3 x^{2}}\\right)\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186495331 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b0a1ddb6-d787-5272-8da2-f78c574a0057" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(y\\cdot \\left(x^{2}\\right)\\right)=\\left(x^{2}\\right)\\cdot \\left(x e^{- 3 x^{2}}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495354} {:answer/id #uuid "b2edb963-4daf-598e-816b-c5cb6ed428ba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(y\\cdot \\left(e^{6 x}\\right)\\right)=\\left(e^{6 x}\\right)\\cdot \\left(x e^{- 3 x^{2}}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495355} {:answer/id #uuid "d6c4ecd7-45d3-5286-be1d-4b5239069918" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(y\\cdot \\left(e^{3 x}\\right)\\right)=\\left(e^{3 x}\\right)\\cdot \\left(x e^{- 3 x^{2}}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495362} {:answer/id #uuid "d874a698-ec62-5e57-b47f-d2f87188207b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(y\\cdot \\left(e^{3 x^{2}}\\right)\\right)=\\left(e^{3 x^{2}}\\right)\\cdot \\left(x e^{- 3 x^{2}}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495363} {:answer/id #uuid "da12d361-8838-591b-bfa5-7ded0d694cc8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(y\\cdot \\left(e^{- 3 x^{2}}\\right)\\right)=\\left(e^{- 3 x^{2}}\\right)\\cdot \\left(x e^{- 3 x^{2}}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495364}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d874a698-ec62-5e57-b47f-d2f87188207b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(y\\cdot \\left(e^{3 x^{2}}\\right)\\right)=\\left(e^{3 x^{2}}\\right)\\cdot \\left(x e^{- 3 x^{2}}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495363} :answer-field/id #uuid "a2c984ae-4255-58f2-8e93-17123c168a48" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495351}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "5fc70cd8-a2b7-5ba8-8458-979a4da1da5f" :question/problem "Consider the following first-order linear ODE for the function $y=y(x):$\n\n$$\n\\left(3\\right)\\cdot \\frac{dy}{dx}+\\left(18 x\\right)\\cdot y=3 x e^{- 3 x^{2}}\n$$\n\nWrite the equation in the form $\\frac{d}{dx}(yI(x))=I(x)Q(x),$ where $I(x)$ is an integrating factor." :question/worked-solution "First, we write the equation in standard form. This gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}+\\left(6 x\\right)\\cdot y=x e^{- 3 x^{2}}.\n$$\n\nThis equation is in the standard form\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}+P(x)y=Q(x)\n$$\n\nwith $P(x)=6 x$ and $Q(x)=x e^{- 3 x^{2}}.$ We proceed to find an integrating factor $I(x)$ using the definition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x) & =e^{\\int P(x)\\,dx} \\\\  & =e^{\\int \\left(6 x\\right)\\,dx} \\\\  & =e^{3 x^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply our differential equation through by $I(x)=e^{3 x^{2}}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\left(e^{3 x^{2}}\\right)\\cdot \\left(\\frac{dy}{dx}+\\left(6 x\\right)\\cdot y\\right) & =\\left(e^{3 x^{2}}\\right)\\cdot \\left(x e^{- 3 x^{2}}\\right) \\\\ \\left(e^{3 x^{2}}\\right)\\cdot \\frac{dy}{dx}+\\left(6 x\\right)\\cdot \\left(e^{3 x^{2}}\\right)\\cdot y & =\\left(e^{3 x^{2}}\\right)\\cdot \\left(x e^{- 3 x^{2}}\\right)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we rewrite the left hand side as $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y\\cdot I(x)):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(y\\cdot \\left(e^{3 x^{2}}\\right)\\right) & =\\left(e^{3 x^{2}}\\right)\\cdot \\left(x e^{- 3 x^{2}}\\right)\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186495346 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "12a0cb4c-5470-5b60-b845-2fea9caa9516" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(y\\cdot \\left(x\\right)\\right)=\\left(x\\right)\\cdot \\left(x^{2}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495314} {:answer/id #uuid "732634a7-b684-5342-875a-b0080faf8912" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(y\\cdot \\left(e^{x}\\right)\\right)=\\left(e^{x}\\right)\\cdot \\left(x^{2}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495335} {:answer/id #uuid "91971313-09d0-59d7-a70f-11595c40eb04" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(y\\cdot \\left(e^{2 x}\\right)\\right)=\\left(e^{2 x}\\right)\\cdot \\left(x^{2}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495344} {:answer/id #uuid "a06cec39-9592-52fd-a2e7-778b2eb94b1a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(y\\cdot \\left(x^{2}\\right)\\right)=\\left(x^{2}\\right)\\cdot \\left(x^{2}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495349} {:answer/id #uuid "c88c1c16-6052-5ee3-ad30-dc668b434dc8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(y\\cdot \\left(e^{- x}\\right)\\right)=\\left(e^{- x}\\right)\\cdot \\left(x^{2}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495360}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "732634a7-b684-5342-875a-b0080faf8912" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(y\\cdot \\left(e^{x}\\right)\\right)=\\left(e^{x}\\right)\\cdot \\left(x^{2}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495335} :answer-field/id #uuid "3060f3c4-885b-5427-ae2c-0db77cc62040" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495323}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "979f5ce5-340c-5f1b-87a2-e39d8a750547" :question/problem "Consider the following first-order linear ODE for the function $y=y(x):$\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}+y=x^{2}\n$$\n\nWrite the equation in the form $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(yI(x))=I(x)Q(x),$ where $I(x)$ is an integrating factor." :question/worked-solution "This equation is in the standard form\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}+P(x)y=Q(x)\n$$\n\nwith $P(x)=1$ and $Q(x)=x^{2}.$ We proceed to find an integrating factor $I(x)$ using the definition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x) & =e^{\\int P(x)\\,dx} \\\\  & =e^{\\int \\left(1\\right)\\,dx} \\\\  & =e^{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply our differential equation through by $I(x)=e^{x}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\left(e^{x}\\right)\\cdot \\left(\\frac{dy}{dx}+y\\right) & =\\left(e^{x}\\right)\\cdot \\left(x^{2}\\right) \\\\ \\left(e^{x}\\right)\\cdot \\frac{dy}{dx}+\\left(1\\right)\\cdot \\left(e^{x}\\right)\\cdot y & =\\left(e^{x}\\right)\\cdot \\left(x^{2}\\right)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we rewrite the left hand side as $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y\\cdot I(x)):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(y\\cdot \\left(e^{x}\\right)\\right) & =\\left(e^{x}\\right)\\cdot \\left(x^{2}\\right)\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186495352 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "06ad0058-543a-56f0-a30b-63445b19fb0b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(y\\cdot \\left(e^{2 x^{2}}\\right)\\right)=\\left(e^{2 x^{2}}\\right)\\cdot \\left(x e^{2 x^{2}}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495313} {:answer/id #uuid "691137d8-cd1d-5c0e-9f2b-2a806bb36f04" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(y\\cdot \\left(e^{- 4 x}\\right)\\right)=\\left(e^{- 4 x}\\right)\\cdot \\left(x e^{2 x^{2}}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495333} {:answer/id #uuid "78cff9f9-81d3-58d9-80de-61ed3308bf21" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(y\\cdot \\left(x^{2}\\right)\\right)=\\left(x^{2}\\right)\\cdot \\left(x e^{2 x^{2}}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495338} {:answer/id #uuid "a0d2a8ac-88e4-519a-a1cd-67d2fbbb3352" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(y\\cdot \\left(e^{- 2 x^{2}}\\right)\\right)=\\left(e^{- 2 x^{2}}\\right)\\cdot \\left(x e^{2 x^{2}}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495350} {:answer/id #uuid "c0f3de7a-6564-5867-82e4-70f297fecd6f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(y\\cdot \\left(e^{- 2 x}\\right)\\right)=\\left(e^{- 2 x}\\right)\\cdot \\left(x e^{2 x^{2}}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495359}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a0d2a8ac-88e4-519a-a1cd-67d2fbbb3352" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(y\\cdot \\left(e^{- 2 x^{2}}\\right)\\right)=\\left(e^{- 2 x^{2}}\\right)\\cdot \\left(x e^{2 x^{2}}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495350} :answer-field/id #uuid "69a0153e-e665-5303-b863-b688cef26fcb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495334}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "a93a7e39-a731-543f-a963-6e7df8a6a066" :question/problem "Consider the following first-order linear ODE for the function $y=y(x):$\n\n$$\n\\left(3\\right)\\cdot \\frac{dy}{dx}-\\left(12 x\\right)\\cdot y=3 x e^{2 x^{2}}\n$$\n\nWrite the equation in the form $\\frac{d}{dx}(yI(x))=I(x)Q(x),$ where $I(x)$ is an integrating factor." :question/worked-solution "First, we write the equation in standard form. This gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}-\\left(4 x\\right)\\cdot y=x e^{2 x^{2}}.\n$$\n\nThis equation is in the standard form\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}+P(x)y=Q(x)\n$$\n\nwith $P(x)=- 4 x$ and $Q(x)=x e^{2 x^{2}}.$ We proceed to find an integrating factor $I(x)$ using the definition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x) & =e^{\\int P(x)\\,dx} \\\\  & =e^{\\int \\left(- 4 x\\right)\\,dx} \\\\  & =e^{- 2 x^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply our differential equation through by $I(x)=e^{- 2 x^{2}}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\left(e^{- 2 x^{2}}\\right)\\cdot \\left(\\frac{dy}{dx}-\\left(4 x\\right)\\cdot y\\right) & =\\left(e^{- 2 x^{2}}\\right)\\cdot \\left(x e^{2 x^{2}}\\right) \\\\ \\left(e^{- 2 x^{2}}\\right)\\cdot \\frac{dy}{dx}-\\left(4 x\\right)\\cdot \\left(e^{- 2 x^{2}}\\right)\\cdot y & =\\left(e^{- 2 x^{2}}\\right)\\cdot \\left(x e^{2 x^{2}}\\right)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we rewrite the left hand side as $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y\\cdot I(x)):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(y\\cdot \\left(e^{- 2 x^{2}}\\right)\\right) & =\\left(e^{- 2 x^{2}}\\right)\\cdot \\left(x e^{2 x^{2}}\\right)\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186495365 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "201b36fa-0814-5d00-973f-9ea16b2c7bfe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(y\\cdot \\left(e^{x^{3}}\\right)\\right)=\\left(e^{x^{3}}\\right)\\cdot \\left(- 2 x^{2} e^{- x^{3}}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495316} {:answer/id #uuid "248f9da1-4a90-5cc6-a0a1-8f0e57ae0b38" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(y\\cdot \\left(e^{x^{2}}\\right)\\right)=\\left(e^{x^{2}}\\right)\\cdot \\left(- 2 x^{2} e^{- x^{3}}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495318} {:answer/id #uuid "3f0917b2-e171-5519-aaea-a9656225eb5d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(y\\cdot \\left(e^{3 x^{2}}\\right)\\right)=\\left(e^{3 x^{2}}\\right)\\cdot \\left(- 2 x^{2} e^{- x^{3}}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495324} {:answer/id #uuid "86f8e704-c271-54b0-8f3b-f19b74aa73d1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(y\\cdot \\left(x^{3}\\right)\\right)=\\left(x^{3}\\right)\\cdot \\left(- 2 x^{2} e^{- x^{3}}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495343} {:answer/id #uuid "f069259a-bb7f-547f-b153-6929fbc00168" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(y\\cdot \\left(e^{- x^{3}}\\right)\\right)=\\left(e^{- x^{3}}\\right)\\cdot \\left(- 2 x^{2} e^{- x^{3}}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495368}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "201b36fa-0814-5d00-973f-9ea16b2c7bfe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(y\\cdot \\left(e^{x^{3}}\\right)\\right)=\\left(e^{x^{3}}\\right)\\cdot \\left(- 2 x^{2} e^{- x^{3}}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495316} :answer-field/id #uuid "576e7528-98ed-5b0c-a3c9-95b0d86f76aa" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495329}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "e16136e3-d19b-5d0f-ac52-7fc12ecac0e5" :question/problem "Consider the following first-order linear ODE for the function $y=y(x):$\n\n$$\n\\left(4\\right)\\cdot \\frac{dy}{dx}+\\left(12 x^{2}\\right)\\cdot y=- 8 x^{2} e^{- x^{3}}\n$$\n\nWrite the equation in the form $\\frac{d}{dx}(yI(x))=I(x)Q(x),$ where $I(x)$ is an integrating factor." :question/worked-solution "First, we write the equation in standard form. This gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}+\\left(3 x^{2}\\right)\\cdot y=- 2 x^{2} e^{- x^{3}}.\n$$\n\nThis equation is in the standard form\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}+P(x)y=Q(x)\n$$\n\nwith $P(x)=3 x^{2}$ and $Q(x)=- 2 x^{2} e^{- x^{3}}.$ We proceed to find an integrating factor $I(x)$ using the definition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x) & =e^{\\int P(x)\\,dx} \\\\  & =e^{\\int \\left(3 x^{2}\\right)\\,dx} \\\\  & =e^{x^{3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply our differential equation through by $I(x)=e^{x^{3}}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\left(e^{x^{3}}\\right)\\cdot \\left(\\frac{dy}{dx}+\\left(3 x^{2}\\right)\\cdot y\\right) & =\\left(e^{x^{3}}\\right)\\cdot \\left(- 2 x^{2} e^{- x^{3}}\\right) \\\\ \\left(e^{x^{3}}\\right)\\cdot \\frac{dy}{dx}+\\left(3 x^{2}\\right)\\cdot \\left(e^{x^{3}}\\right)\\cdot y & =\\left(e^{x^{3}}\\right)\\cdot \\left(- 2 x^{2} e^{- x^{3}}\\right)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we rewrite the left hand side as $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y\\cdot I(x)):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(y\\cdot \\left(e^{x^{3}}\\right)\\right) & =\\left(e^{x^{3}}\\right)\\cdot \\left(- 2 x^{2} e^{- x^{3}}\\right)\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186495370 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5148fd6c-572e-5d2c-8376-11bdb4050d85" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(y\\cdot \\left(e^{9 x^{2}}\\right)\\right)=\\left(e^{9 x^{2}}\\right)\\cdot \\left(x^{2} e^{- 3 x^{3}}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495326} {:answer/id #uuid "74fed037-bc3c-52e9-8724-6cd409b9d803" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(y\\cdot \\left(e^{3 x^{3}}\\right)\\right)=\\left(e^{3 x^{3}}\\right)\\cdot \\left(x^{2} e^{- 3 x^{3}}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495337} {:answer/id #uuid "eef79248-81ac-5c45-9664-a05bf9892e48" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(y\\cdot \\left(x^{3}\\right)\\right)=\\left(x^{3}\\right)\\cdot \\left(x^{2} e^{- 3 x^{3}}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495367} {:answer/id #uuid "fe45a64f-3142-59f9-ba22-04ea27f572a8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(y\\cdot \\left(e^{- 3 x^{3}}\\right)\\right)=\\left(e^{- 3 x^{3}}\\right)\\cdot \\left(x^{2} e^{- 3 x^{3}}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495372} {:answer/id #uuid "fe5d7112-8717-5010-8fb1-6e72bf176e8f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(y\\cdot \\left(e^{3 x^{2}}\\right)\\right)=\\left(e^{3 x^{2}}\\right)\\cdot \\left(x^{2} e^{- 3 x^{3}}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495373}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "74fed037-bc3c-52e9-8724-6cd409b9d803" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(y\\cdot \\left(e^{3 x^{3}}\\right)\\right)=\\left(e^{3 x^{3}}\\right)\\cdot \\left(x^{2} e^{- 3 x^{3}}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495337} :answer-field/id #uuid "9e410e0d-8c34-5eae-a523-dcd96b802712" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495348}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "f836cacf-c820-5e10-bdf7-7e25abb1df90" :question/problem "Consider the following first-order linear ODE for the function $y=y(x):$\n\n$$\n\\left(4\\right)\\cdot \\frac{dy}{dx}+\\left(36 x^{2}\\right)\\cdot y=4 x^{2} e^{- 3 x^{3}}\n$$\n\nWrite the equation in the form $\\frac{d}{dx}(yI(x))=I(x)Q(x),$ where $I(x)$ is an integrating factor." :question/worked-solution "First, we write the equation in standard form. This gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}+\\left(9 x^{2}\\right)\\cdot y=x^{2} e^{- 3 x^{3}}.\n$$\n\nThis equation is in the standard form\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}+P(x)y=Q(x)\n$$\n\nwith $P(x)=9 x^{2}$ and $Q(x)=x^{2} e^{- 3 x^{3}}.$ We proceed to find an integrating factor $I(x)$ using the definition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x) & =e^{\\int P(x)\\,dx} \\\\  & =e^{\\int \\left(9 x^{2}\\right)\\,dx} \\\\  & =e^{3 x^{3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply our differential equation through by $I(x)=e^{3 x^{3}}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\left(e^{3 x^{3}}\\right)\\cdot \\left(\\frac{dy}{dx}+\\left(9 x^{2}\\right)\\cdot y\\right) & =\\left(e^{3 x^{3}}\\right)\\cdot \\left(x^{2} e^{- 3 x^{3}}\\right) \\\\ \\left(e^{3 x^{3}}\\right)\\cdot \\frac{dy}{dx}+\\left(9 x^{2}\\right)\\cdot \\left(e^{3 x^{3}}\\right)\\cdot y & =\\left(e^{3 x^{3}}\\right)\\cdot \\left(x^{2} e^{- 3 x^{3}}\\right)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we rewrite the left hand side as $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y\\cdot I(x)):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(y\\cdot \\left(e^{3 x^{3}}\\right)\\right) & =\\left(e^{3 x^{3}}\\right)\\cdot \\left(x^{2} e^{- 3 x^{3}}\\right)\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Transforming First-Order Linear ODEs Using Integrating Factors"}]}
